    "created_at": "2024-01-08T22:31:14Z",
    "updated_at": "2024-01-08T22:31:14Z",
    "body": "> WebKit and Blink probably do the same (clipping internally?).\r\n\r\nIt is clipped internally. Confusingly, it's [explicitly set](https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:third_party/blink/renderer/core/html/resources/html.css;l=977;drc=95f430edbf3e33525b4ac122875360b8d44c0630) to `overflow:visible` in the UA stylesheet.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n> @mfreed7 @nt1m do you know how WebKit / Blink make listbox scrollable?\r\n\r\nI believe this is via [this UA stylesheet rule](https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:third_party/blink/renderer/core/html/resources/html.css;l=970;drc=95f430edbf3e33525b4ac122875360b8d44c0630).\r\n\r\nRationalizing all of this, if it can be done interoperably, sounds good to me.",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
